;
WHEN THINGS DON'T WORK

A - When things don't work as expected

:A
WHEN THINGS DON'T WORK AS EXPECTED

Symptom - Things to try
  No connection - Check the advertised address and port; the board may be
  occupied
  Connected, but no welcome - Check Raw TCP and press RETURN
  A directory name is missing - Check the mounted volume and use its numeric
  DU
  A command is rejected - Check spelling, DU and caller execution approval
  Download appears to stall - Start the matching YMODEM receive operation
  Uploaded file isn't in DIR - Expected: the submission is in the private
  sysop inbox
  RBBS ignores RETURN - Normal menus use single-key selection
  CHAT or Maze Chase display is garbled - Check ANSI/VT100 and terminal
  dimensions; CHAT /S is an alternative for chat
  Saved game is gone - WORK is temporary and cleared between calls

If you can't resolve a difficulty, leave the sysop a note. Include the steps
needed to reproduce it rather than merely saying that the program doesn't
work.
